      arabic: "يَا مُقَلِّبَ الْقُلُوبِ ثَبِّتْ قَلْبِي عَلَى دِينِكَ",
      translit: "Yā Muqallibal-qulūb, thabbit qalbī ʿalā dīnik.",
      meaning: "O Turner of hearts, keep my heart firm on Your religion.",
      gloss: "My father-in-law had said this du'a through the splintering. I said it through the ordinary years. A keeping, said over and over until it becomes the shape of a life.",
